  "prefLabel": "Jus 2001.05 “Chief medical examiner” (CME) means the licensed physician certified by the American Board of Pathology as a qualified pathologist and appointed pursuant to RS",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Jus 2001.05 “Chief medical examiner” (CME) means the licensed physician certified by the American Board of Pathology as a qualified pathologist and appointed pursuant to RSA 611-A:1, I, to investigate deaths and supervise the office of chief medical examiner.\n\nSource. #8937, eff 7-14-07",
